---
/* spring-fest.html — section 7 of 10.

   What the price covers, what it does not, and what happens to the
   money if somebody cancels. All of it transcribed from the brochures
   in asset/iit kgp/, including the qualifier on the refund slabs —
   they apply to the refundable portion, after non-refundable costs are
   taken out — because that sentence is the difference between what
   somebody expects back and what actually arrives.

   NOTE(mannat): these slabs are Spring Fest's own and they are NOT the
   ones on /cancellation-policy, which says 80 / 50 / 0 across three
   windows. The brochure says 75 / 50 / 25 / 0 across four. Both are now
   published, each labelled with what it covers, and the policy page
   carries a line pointing here. Confirm which one governs Spring Fest
   and we will make the other match. */
---

<section class="sec s-white">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="slug"><b>06</b><span>One price, everything below</span><span class="ln"></span><span class="m hide-s">The fine print</span></p>
    <div class="split end">
      <h2 class="d-l" data-split style="max-width:12ch">What you’re <span class="it">actually getting</span></h2>
      <p class="lede">₹2,499 to lock your seat, confirmed once we confirm it, the balance due by 22 December, 30 days before the fest</p>
    </div>

    <div class="split mt-64">
      <div class="stack">
        <span class="label">In the price</span>
        <ul class="forl" style="margin-top:14px">
          <li>Pickup and drop, Howrah or Kharagpur station</li>
          <li>Four nights in an IIT Kharagpur hostel</li>
          <li>Every meal, dinner on the 21st to the last one</li>
          <li>Your Spring Fest pass, all three fest days</li>
          <li>A trip captain, the whole way</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <span class="label">Not in the price</span>
        <ul class="forl" style="margin-top:14px">
          <li>Your train or flight, we help you book it</li>
          <li>Personal spending outside the meal plan</li>
          <li>Anything not listed on this page</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="body muted">Rail bookings open 60 days ahead, around 22 November 2026 for a 21 January arrival, book early or ask us</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-96">
      <span class="label">If you cancel · Spring Fest 2027</span>
      <div class="facts mt-24">
        <div class="fact"><small>30+ days before</small><b class="tabular">75%</b></div>
        <div class="fact"><small>15 – 29 days before</small><b class="tabular">50%</b></div>
        <div class="fact"><small>7 – 14 days before</small><b class="tabular">25%</b></div>
        <div class="fact"><small>0 – 6 days before</small><b class="tabular">0%</b></div>
      </div>
      <p class="fine mt-24">Days are counted back from 21 January 2027, the day of pickup. The percentages apply to the refundable portion, after non-refundable costs such as entry tickets are taken out. No show, no refund. If we cancel the departure, you get all of it back. You can pass your spot to another eligible person with our approval. These windows are Spring Fest’s own, the rest of the terms are in the <a class="under" href="cancellation-policy.html">cancellation policy</a> and the <a class="under" href="terms.html">terms of travel</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
